{
  "dom_id": "step-q81562",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Let $A$ and $B$ be the set of all multiples of $4$ greater than $0$ and the set of all multiples of $5$ greater than $0,$ respectively. What is $A\\cup B?$",
  "worked_solution": "The multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA=\\{4,8,12,16,20,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $5$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB=\\{5,10,15,20,…\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, $A\\cup B$ is the *union* of $A$ and $B,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in either $A$ or $B,$ or both. In other words, $A\\cup B$ denotes the set of natural numbers that are either multiple of $4$ or multiple of $5.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cup B & =\\{4,8,12,16,20,…\\}\\cup \\{5,10,15,20,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{4,5,8,10,12,15,16,20,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
